> API and interpretation

The native maximum is the largest original-vertex distance to its assigned
retained chord. It upper-bounds distance to the union of all retained chords and
is not necessarily that union nearest-distance maximum. Endpoint clamping
intentionally corrects the old infinite-supporting-line behavior: the collinear
path0 to2 to1 retains its overshoot at epsilon0.5. Every coordinate and epsilon
is checked even on short input; arithmetic beyond finite double range throws.
The waveform is a native synthetic structural input, not a geographic dataset or
a topology guarantee.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Ramer, An iterative procedure for polygonal approximation of plane curves (1972)|https://doi.org/10.1016/S0146-664X(72)80017-0]
- [Douglas and Peucker, Algorithms for the Reduction of the Number of Points (1973)|https://doi.org/10.3138/FM57-6770-U75U-7727]

